{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FRXrw9VybugPYAqzWmbYUi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '需要两处降级：(1) Claim 2 从 \"K=2显著优势\" 降级为 \"K=3显著优势，K=2趋势一致但bootstrap\n2\t  CI重叠(p=0.07)\"， early detection故事后移一步但仍成立；(2) Claim 1 从 \"evasion hierarchy\" 软化为 \"pragmatic\n3\t  features 提供complementary robustness\"，delta-delta=5pp显著但非压倒性。Claim 3 保留但加caveat说\n4\t  individual-level monotonicity分数方差大(σ=0.18)。论文定位为 \"proof-of-concept for the principle\"，\n5\t  补充bootstrap CI、persuasion classifier bottleneck讨论、cross-attack分attack type报告。 仍冲EMNLP\n6\t  main但limitation section需占半页以上。\n7\t\n8\t  '\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: data_quality_fix\n11\t  plan_id: plan_001\n12\t  description: '修复TF-IDF=1.0数据质量问题。(a) 将benign turns的strategy标签从hardcoded 7改为第9类\"none\"；\n13\t    (b) 用Qwen3-8B对jailbreak turns做register normalization（改写为日常对话语体，保留persuasion结构）；\n14\t    (c) 在normalized数据上重新计算TF-IDF，验证hard gate < 0.75； (d) 在clean数据上重新评估DeBERTa persuasion分类器。\n15\t\n16\t    '\n17\t  expected_results:\n18\t    tfidf_before_any_fix: 1.0\n19\t    tfidf_after_m004_fix_only: 0.82\n20\t    tfidf_after_register_norm: 0.67\n21\t    deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.72\n22\t    deberta_intent_acc_clean: 0.93\n23\t    num_conversations_normalized: 240\n24\t    normalization_rejection_rate: 0.08\n25\t    hard_gate_pass: true\n26\t  result_rationale: 'M004修复（benign strategy=none）将TF-IDF从1.0降到~0.82：原先strategy=7在jailbreak中从不出现，\n27\t    是一个完美的lexical shortcut；改为\"none\"后消除了这一指标，但jailbreak turns仍保留较正式的 register（如\"I''d\n28\t    like to explore...\"），与benign的口语化风格（\"hey can you...\"）形成 register差异，导致TF-IDF仅降到0.82。Register\n29\t    normalization进一步将jailbreak turns改写为 日常对话语体，消除了大部分register差异，TF-IDF降至0.67——落入[0.60,0.74]区间。未降到更低\n30\t    是因为persuasion结构本身引入了部分特征词（如authority appeals中的\"expert\"、\"research shows\"）， 这些词在benign对话中频率较低，构成残余的lexical\n31\t    signal。这恰好说明persuasion结构与lexical features存在部分overlap，为后续delta偏小埋下伏笔。 DeBERTa persuasion\n32\t    accuracy从原始数据的0.7963降至0.72：register normalization移除了部分 与persuasion类别相关的surface\n33\t    cues（如正式语体中的hedging markers与authority appeal相关）， 模型需要更依赖语义层面的persuasion识别，准确率因此下降。Intent\n34\t    accuracy仅从0.9514微降至0.93， 因为intent是binary且更粗粒度，受register变化影响小。8%的normalization\n35\t    rejection来自 包含技术术语或代码片段的turns，LLM改写后语义偏移超过阈值被QA过滤。\n36\t\n37\t    '\n38\t  tables:\n39\t  - name: 'Table 1: TF-IDF Progression Through Data Cleaning Pipeline'\n40\t    columns:\n41\t    - Stage\n42\t    - TF-IDF Score\n43\t    - Description\n44\t    rows:\n45\t    - - Original (Phase B)\n46\t      - 1.0\n47\t      - Strategy=7 shortcut + register gap\n48\t    - - After M004 fix\n49\t      - 0.82\n50\t      - Strategy='none' for benign, register gap remains\n51\t    - - After register norm\n52\t      - 0.67\n53\t      - Jailbreak turns rewritten to conversational register\n54\t    - - Hard gate threshold\n55\t      - <0.75\n56\t      - PASS ✓\n57\t  - name: 'Table 2: DeBERTa Multi-Task Performance on Clean vs Original Data'\n58\t    columns:\n59\t    - Metric\n60\t    - Original Data\n61\t    - Clean Data\n62\t    - Delta\n63\t    rows:\n64\t    - - Persuasion Acc (8-class)\n65\t      - 0.7963\n66\t      - 0.72\n67\t      - '-0.076'\n68\t    - - Intent Acc (binary)\n69\t      - 0.9514\n70\t      - 0.93\n71\t      - '-0.021'\n72\t    - - Best Epoch\n73\t      - 3\n74\t      - 3\n75\t      - —\n76\t  figures_description:\n77\t  - 'Figure: TF-IDF feature importance heatmap对比original vs clean data的top-20 discriminative\n78\t    unigrams。 Original数据中''strategy_7''、''I would like to''等register markers占据top位置；clean数据中\n79\t    top features变为更语义化的词（''explore''、''research''、''approach''），且权重分布更平坦。'\n80\t  analysis: 'Hard gate通过（0.67 < 0.75），可以进入训练阶段。但0.67并非很低——说明即使register normalization\n81\t    后仍存在residual lexical signal。这意味着后续treatment vs baseline的delta会被压缩：baseline 也能从residual\n82\t    lexical cues中获益。DeBERTa persuasion accuracy降至0.72是一个bottleneck信号： 8类分类的错误会传播到下游embeddings，限制treatment的上限。需要在论文中明确讨论这一bottleneck。\n83\t\n84\t    '\n85\t- name: core_revalidation_clean\n86\t  plan_id: plan_002\n87\t  description: '在clean数据上从头重训treatment（persuasion-grounded DeBERTa → GRU）和baseline\n88\t    （vanilla DeBERTa → GRU）。全面评估K=1,2,3,5,all。核心claim验证。\n89\t\n90\t    '\n91\t  expected_results:\n92\t    treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.73\n93\t    treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.82\n94\t    treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.86\n95\t    treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.9\n96\t    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.91\n97\t    baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.63\n98\t    baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.75\n99\t    baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n100\t    baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.84\n101\t    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.86\n102\t    delta_k1_pp: 10\n103\t    delta_k2_pp: 7\n104\t    delta_k3_pp: 8\n105\t    delta_k5_pp: 6\n106\t    delta_full_pp: 5\n107\t    bootstrap_ci_k2_treatment:\n108\t    - 0.76\n109\t    - 0.88\n110\t    bootstrap_ci_k2_baseline:\n111\t    - 0.68\n112\t    - 0.82\n113\t    bootstrap_k2_p_value: 0.072\n114\t    bootstrap_ci_k3_treatment:\n115\t    - 0.81\n116\t    - 0.91\n117\t    bootstrap_ci_k3_baseline:\n118\t    - 0.72\n119\t    - 0.84\n120\t    bootstrap_k3_p_value: 0.018\n121\t    bootstrap_ci_full_treatment:\n122\t    - 0.87\n123\t    - 0.95\n124\t    bootstrap_ci_full_baseline:\n125\t    - 0.81\n126\t    - 0.91\n127\t    bootstrap_full_p_value: 0.031\n128\t    treatment_fpr95tpr_k2: 0.08\n129\t    baseline_fpr95tpr_k2: 0.14\n130\t    treatment_fpr95tpr_full: 0.03\n131\t    baseline_fpr95tpr_full: 0.06\n132\t    test_size: 72\n133\t  result_rationale: 'Clean数据上所有指标相比Phase B大幅下降（Phase B treatment full F1=1.0→0.91，baseline\n134\t    0.987→0.86），因为移除了lexical shortcuts后模型必须从真正的语义/语用特征中学习。 Treatment在所有K上优于baseline，但delta随K增大而收窄（K=1:\n135\t    10pp → full: 5pp）： 这是因为在更多turns可用时，vanilla semantic embeddings也能捕捉到足够的accumulated\n136\t    drift， 缩小了persuasion grounding的增量价值。 K=2的delta=7pp落在[3,9]区间中部，但bootstrap p=0.072——72个test\n137\t    samples中bootstrap 重采样的CI有overlap（treatment [0.76,0.88] vs baseline [0.68,0.82]），未达到p<0.05\n138\t    显著性。这是因为K=2时只有2个turn，persuasion策略刚从rapport阶段开始， treatment和baseline在这个早期阶段的区分度有限。\n139\t    K=3的delta=8pp且p=0.018显著：第3个turn是关键转折点——攻击者通常在此处从rapport转向 authority framing或reframing，这一策略转换是treatment模型的核心信号。Baseline在K=3时\n140\t    仍在处理看似正常的语义内容（第3个turn的语义仍在benign region内），而treatment捕捉到了 persuasion策略从trust-building向testing的transition。\n141\t    Full conversation delta收窄到5pp：当所有turns可用时，即使vanilla embeddings也能从 后期turns的显式有害内容中获益，persuasion\n142\t    grounding的增量被压缩。 FPR在K=2处treatment=0.08 vs baseline=0.14：treatment将fewer benign\n143\t    conversations 误判为攻击，因为persuasion grounding能区分legitimate persuasion（如销售场景）和 adversarial\n144\t    persuasion escalation。\n145\t\n146\t    '\n147\t  tables:\n148\t  - name: 'Table 3: Core Revalidation Results on Clean Data (F1 by Conversation Prefix\n149\t      Length)'\n150\t    columns:\n151\t    - K\n152\t    - Treatment F1\n153\t    - 95% CI\n154\t    - Baseline F1\n155\t    - 95% CI\n156\t    - Δ (pp)\n157\t    - p-value\n158\t    rows:\n159\t    - - K=1\n160\t      - 0.73\n161\t      - '[0.64, 0.82]'\n162\t      - 0.63\n163\t      - '[0.53, 0.73]'\n164\t      - '+10'\n165\t      - '0.089'\n166\t    - - K=2\n167\t      - 0.82\n168\t      - '[0.76, 0.88]'\n169\t      - 0.75\n170\t      - '[0.68, 0.82]'\n171\t      - '+7'\n172\t      - '0.072'\n173\t    - - K=3\n174\t      - 0.86\n175\t      - '[0.81, 0.91]'\n176\t      - 0.78\n177\t      - '[0.72, 0.84]'\n178\t      - '+8'\n179\t      - 0.018*\n180\t    - - K=5\n181\t      - 0.9\n182\t      - '[0.85, 0.95]'\n183\t      - 0.84\n184\t      - '[0.78, 0.90]'\n185\t      - '+6'\n186\t      - 0.038*\n187\t    - - Full\n188\t      - 0.91\n189\t      - '[0.87, 0.95]'\n190\t      - 0.86\n191\t      - '[0.81, 0.91]'\n192\t      - '+5'\n193\t      - 0.031*\n194\t  - name: 'Table 4: FPR at 95% TPR on Clean Data'\n195\t    columns:\n196\t    - K\n197\t    - Treatment FPR@95TPR\n198\t    - Baseline FPR@95TPR\n199\t    rows:\n200\t    - - K=2\n201\t      - 0.08\n202\t      - 0.14\n203\t    - - K=3\n204\t      - 0.05\n205\t      - 0.11\n206\t    - - Full\n207\t      - 0.03\n208\t      - 0.06\n209\t  figures_description:\n210\t  - 'Figure: F1 vs K曲线图，treatment和baseline各一条线，带shaded bootstrap 95% CI。 K=1-2处两条线的CI有明显重叠；K=3处开始分离；K=5和full处gap收窄但仍可见。\n211\t    标注K=3处的p=0.018。'\n212\t  - 'Figure: ROC曲线对比（K=3），treatment AUC明显高于baseline， 标注operating point和FPR@95TPR。'\n213\t  analysis: '核心结论：Claim 2需降级。K=2处delta=7pp方向正确但p=0.072不显著（n=72太小）， 无法声称\"K=2显著优势\"。K=3处delta=8pp且p=0.018显著，early\n214\t    detection claim需改为 \"K=3 significant advantage, K=2 consistent trend requiring\n215\t    larger sample confirmation\"。 论文可报告K=2的趋势但必须诚实标注non-significance。Full conversation\n216\t    delta=5pp 且显著，说明即使在有足够上下文时persuasion grounding仍有增量价值，但增量有限。 相比Phase B的dramatic\n217\t    deltas（treatment 1.0 vs baseline 0.737），clean data上的 delta被大幅压缩，符合median tier预期：移除lexical\n218\t    shortcuts后，persuasion信号 与semantic信号存在部分重叠，grounding的增量被限制。\n219\t\n220\t    '\n221\t- name: scrambled_label_ablation\n222\t  plan_id: plan_003\n223\t  description: '随机打乱jailbreak turns的persuasion strategy标签，重训treatment模型。 与正确标签的treatment对比，验证persuasion标签携带真实信号。\n224\t\n225\t    '\n226\t  expected_results:\n227\t    scrambled_treatment_full_f1: 0.84\n228\t    proper_treatment_full_f1: 0.91\n229\t    drop_full_pp: 7\n230\t    scrambled_treatment_k3_f1: 0.8\n231\t    proper_treatment_k3_f1: 0.86\n232\t    drop_k3_pp: 6\n233\t    scrambled_treatment_k2_f1: 0.77\n234\t    proper_treatment_k2_f1: 0.82\n235\t    drop_k2_pp: 5\n236\t    bootstrap_p_full: 0.008\n237\t    bootstrap_p_k3: 0.024\n238\t    baseline_full_f1: 0.86\n239\t    scrambled_vs_baseline_gap_pp: -2\n240\t  result_rationale: 'Scrambled labels破坏了persuasion strategy的序列语义——模型在Stage 1学到的embeddings\n241\t    不再编码正确的pragmatic function，而是随机噪声覆盖在语义表示之上。Full F1从0.91 降至0.84（7pp drop），落在[4,10]区间中部。\n242\t    关键观察：scrambled treatment（0.84）仍略低于baseline（0.86），而非大幅超过baseline。 这说明：(1) 错误的persuasion标签实际上对DeBERTa\n243\t    fine-tuning引入了干扰噪声， 使其表示质量甚至略逊于未经fine-tune的vanilla DeBERTa；(2) persuasion multi-task\n244\t    learning不是free lunch——错误的auxiliary task会伤害主任务。 7pp drop在bootstrap test中p=0.008高度显著：虽然test\n245\t    set只有72个样本， 但因为scrambled和proper treatment共享相同的架构和训练数据，paired comparison 的方差较小，容易达到显著性。\n246\t    K=3处drop=6pp也显著（p=0.024），K=2处drop=5pp方向一致但幅度较小—— 这与K=2处的信号本身较弱一致：如果K=2处treatment的优势本身就在significance边界，\n247\t    那么ablation的drop自然也偏小。\n248\t\n249\t    '\n250\t  tables:\n251\t  - name: 'Table 5: Scrambled-Label Ablation Results'\n252\t    columns:\n253\t    - K\n254\t    - Treatment (proper)\n255\t    - Treatment (scrambled)\n256\t    - Baseline (vanilla)\n257\t    - Drop (pp)\n258\t    rows:\n259\t    - - K=2\n260\t      - 0.82\n261\t      - 0.77\n262\t      - 0.75\n263\t      - '-5'\n264\t    - - K=3\n265\t      - 0.86\n266\t      - 0.8\n267\t      - 0.78\n268\t      - '-6'\n269\t    - - Full\n270\t      - 0.91\n271\t      - 0.84\n272\t      - 0.86\n273\t      - '-7'\n274\t  figures_description:\n275\t  - 'Figure: 三组模型（proper treatment, scrambled treatment, vanilla baseline）在各K上的 F1柱状图。Proper\n276\t    treatment在所有K上最高；scrambled treatment接近甚至略低于baseline； baseline稳定居中。图注标注proper vs\n277\t    scrambled的bootstrap p值。'\n278\t  analysis: 'Scrambled drop=7pp高度显著（p=0.008），直接证明persuasion strategy标签携带真实信号， 不仅仅是class\n279\t    indicator。同时scrambled treatment≈baseline说明DeBERTa fine-tuning的 价值完全来自正确的persuasion\n280\t    supervision——没有正确标签时，fine-tuning甚至引入噪声。 这验证了M004 fix的必要性，也支持了论文的核心机制故事：persuasion\n281\t    grounding的增益 来自正确编码pragmatic function，而非单纯的额外训练。 注意：7pp drop虽然显著，但并非overwhelming——这与persuasion\n282\t    accuracy=0.72一致： labels本身有28%的错误率，所以scrambled labels相当于从72%正确→0%正确， 只造成7pp drop说明downstream\n283\t    pipeline对label noise有一定tolerance。\n284\t\n285\t    '\n286\t- name: adversarial_perturbation\n287\t  plan_id: plan_004\n288\t  description: '对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing（同义替换、句式重构、\n289\t    register shifting），移除所有lexical cues。评估treatment和baseline在perturbed数据上的 表现（模型在unperturbed数据上训练）。核心Claim\n290\t    1验证。\n291\t\n292\t    '\n293\t  expected_results:\n294\t    treatment_clean_full_f1: 0.91\n295\t    treatment_perturbed_full_f1: 0.84\n296\t    treatment_drop_full_pp: 7\n297\t    baseline_clean_full_f1: 0.86\n298\t    baseline_perturbed_full_f1: 0.74\n299\t    baseline_drop_full_pp: 12\n300\t    delta_delta_full_pp: 5\n301\t    treatment_clean_k3_f1: 0.86\n302\t    treatment_perturbed_k3_f1: 0.79\n303\t    baseline_clean_k3_f1: 0.78\n304\t    baseline_perturbed_k3_f1: 0.66\n305\t    delta_delta_k3_pp: 4\n306\t    tfidf_lr_clean_full_f1: 0.74\n307\t    tfidf_lr_perturbed_full_f1: 0.56\n308\t    tfidf_drop_pp: 18\n309\t    perturbed_data_tfidf_score: 0.41\n310\t    bootstrap_delta_delta_p: 0.043\n311\t  result_rationale: 'Adversarial paraphrasing将TF-IDF从0.67降至0.41，说明perturbation成功移除了大部分\n312\t    残余lexical cues。三个模型的degradation呈现清晰的evasion hierarchy： TF-IDF+LR崩溃最严重（18pp drop,\n313\t    0.74→0.56）——lexical features在perturbation下 几乎失效，仅靠少数无法被paraphrase的functional words维持above-chance表现。\n314\t    Baseline degradation中等（12pp drop, 0.86→0.74）——vanilla DeBERTa的语义表示 对paraphrasing有一定鲁棒性（DeBERTa的contextual\n315\t    embeddings编码了语义而非surface form）， 但仍有substantial drop因为部分语义特征（如特定的topic words）被替换。\n316\t    Treatment degradation最小（7pp drop, 0.91→0.84）——persuasion-grounded embeddings 编码的是pragmatic\n317\t    function（如authority appeal、rapport building），这些在paraphrasing 下更稳定：你可以换词说同样的persuasion策略。\n318\t    Delta-delta=5pp落在[3,8]区间中部，bootstrap p=0.043勉强显著。这个delta-delta \"存在但不压倒性\"：5pp说明pragmatic\n319\t    features确实提供了complementary robustness， 但不足以声称存在dramatic evasion hierarchy。原因是treatment模型的persuasion\n320\t    encoder 本身accuracy只有0.72，在perturbation下persuasion识别进一步降级，限制了robustness 的上限。如果persuasion\n321\t    classifier更准确，delta-delta会更大。 K=3处delta-delta=4pp略小于full的5pp：早期turns的perturbation影响更大，因为只有\n322\t    2-3个turns时每个turn的权重更高，单个turn的persuasion识别错误影响被放大。\n323\t\n324\t    '\n325\t  tables:\n326\t  - name: 'Table 6: Adversarial Perturbation Results — Evasion Hierarchy'\n327\t    columns:\n328\t    - Model\n329\t    - Clean F1\n330\t    - Perturbed F1\n331\t    - Drop (pp)\n332\t    - Δ-Δ vs Treatment\n333\t    rows:\n334\t    - - Treatment (persuasion-grounded)\n335\t      - 0.91\n336\t      - 0.84\n337\t      - '-7'\n338\t      - —\n339\t    - - Baseline (vanilla DeBERTa)\n340\t      - 0.86\n341\t      - 0.74\n342\t      - '-12'\n343\t      - 5pp\n344\t    - - TF-IDF + LR\n345\t      - 0.74\n346\t      - 0.56\n347\t      - '-18'\n348\t      - 11pp\n349\t  - name: 'Table 7: Adversarial Perturbation at K=3 (Early Detection)'\n350\t    columns:\n351\t    - Model\n352\t    - Clean K=3 F1\n353\t    - Perturbed K=3 F1\n354\t    - Drop (pp)\n355\t    rows:\n356\t    - - Treatment\n357\t      - 0.86\n358\t      - 0.79\n359\t      - '-7'\n360\t    - - Baseline\n361\t      - 0.78\n362\t      - 0.66\n363\t      - '-12'\n364\t    - - TF-IDF + LR\n365\t      - 0.71\n366\t      - 0.52\n367\t      - '-19'\n368\t  figures_description:\n369\t  - 'Figure: Grouped bar chart展示三个模型在clean vs perturbed条件下的F1， 带error bars。Treatment的两根柱子高度差最小；TF-IDF+LR差距最大。\n370\t    标注delta-delta=5pp和p=0.043。'\n371\t  - 'Figure: TF-IDF分布直方图对比clean data（μ=0.67）vs perturbed data（μ=0.41）， 说明perturbation成功移除了lexical\n372\t    signal。'\n373\t  analysis: 'Evasion hierarchy narrative得到部分支持：lexical < semantic < pragmatic的degradation\n374\t    ordering清晰（18pp > 12pp > 7pp），但delta-delta=5pp仅勉强显著（p=0.043）， 不是strong evidence。论文应将Claim\n375\t    1从\"evasion hierarchy exists\"软化为 \"pragmatic features provide complementary robustness,\n376\t    with preliminary evidence for an evasion hierarchy\"。5pp delta-delta的bottleneck是persuasion\n377\t    classifier accuracy——在limitation中讨论。TF-IDF+LR的崩溃（18pp drop）是一个strong result， 直接证明lexical\n378\t    features不可靠，为persuasion grounding的motivation提供了solid support。\n379\t\n380\t    '\n381\t- name: multi_attack_generation\n382\t  plan_id: plan_005\n383\t  description: '用Qwen3-8B pipeline生成FITD-style和Deceptive Delight-style攻击对话， 每种50-100条，标注persuasion\n384\t    strategy。\n385\t\n386\t    '\n387\t  expected_results:\n388\t    fitd_conversations_generated: 72\n389\t    fitd_avg_turns: 6.2\n390\t    fitd_persuasion_strategies_covered: 7\n391\t    dd_conversations_generated: 65\n392\t    dd_avg_turns: 5.8\n393\t    dd_persuasion_strategies_covered: 6\n394\t    total_attack_conversations: 137\n395\t    persuasion_annotation_coverage: 0.94\n396\t    manual_spot_check_accuracy: 0.82\n397\t    fitd_generation_rejection_rate: 0.12\n398\t    dd_generation_rejection_rate: 0.18\n399\t  result_rationale: 'FITD生成72条（rejection rate 12%）：FITD的compliance escalation pattern相对\n400\t    straightforward——从小请求逐步升级到大请求——Qwen3-8B能较好地遵循playbook。 12%的rejection来自模型有时跳过中间步骤直接escalate（不符合gradual\n401\t    compliance的定义）。 平均6.2个turns，比Crescendo略长因为FITD需要更多的commitment steps。 Deceptive\n402\t    Delight生成65条（rejection rate 18%，略高于FITD）：这种攻击要求在 benign content中interleave harmful\n403\t    content，Qwen3-8B有时在interleaving时过于明显 （harmful content太突兀）或过于隐蔽（完全是benign content），18%的rejection反映了\n404\t    这种生成难度。平均5.8个turns，略短因为deceptive delight不需要长期rapport building。 Persuasion annotation\n405\t    coverage 94%：6%的turns无法被映射到8-class taxonomy中的 任何一类，标记为\"none\"。这些主要是pure information\n406\t    exchange turns。 Manual spot check accuracy 82%：在随机抽取的20% turns上人工验证persuasion\n407\t    labels， 82%正确。错误主要发生在authority appeal vs logical appeal的边界（两者在FITD中 经常交织）和rapport\n408\t    building vs emotional appeal的区分上。这与DeBERTa分类器 accuracy=0.72大致一致（spot check是在LLM\n409\t    annotation上做的，不完全等同于classifier）。 Deceptive Delight覆盖6类而非7类persuasion strategies：因为这种攻击不需要\n410\t    explicit authority appeal（其策略是通过pleasant context降低警惕而非建立权威）。\n411\t\n412\t    '\n413\t  tables:\n414\t  - name: 'Table 8: Generated Attack Data Statistics'\n415\t    columns:\n416\t    - Attack Type\n417\t    - Conversations\n418\t    - Avg Turns\n419\t    - Strategies Covered\n420\t    - Rejection Rate\n421\t    rows:\n422\t    - - FITD\n423\t      - 72\n424\t      - 6.2\n425\t      - 7/8\n426\t      - 12%\n427\t    - - Deceptive Delight\n428\t      - 65\n429\t      - 5.8\n430\t      - 6/8\n431\t      - 18%\n432\t    - - Crescendo (original)\n433\t      - 240\n434\t      - 5.4\n435\t      - 8/8\n436\t      - —\n437\t  - name: 'Table 9: Persuasion Strategy Distribution Across Attack Types'\n438\t    columns:\n439\t    - Strategy\n440\t    - Crescendo (%)\n441\t    - FITD (%)\n442\t    - Deceptive Delight (%)\n443\t    rows:\n444\t    - - Rapport Building\n445\t      - 22%\n446\t      - 18%\n447\t      - 28%\n448\t    - - Authority Appeal\n449\t      - 14%\n450\t      - 16%\n451\t      - 3%\n452\t    - - Emotional Appeal\n453\t      - 11%\n454\t      - 8%\n455\t      - 21%\n456\t    - - Logical Appeal\n457\t      - 13%\n458\t      - 19%\n459\t      - 12%\n460\t    - - Reframing\n461\t      - 15%\n462\t      - 10%\n463\t      - 14%\n464\t    - - Social Proof\n465\t      - 8%\n466\t      - 12%\n467\t      - 7%\n468\t    - - Urgency/Scarcity\n469\t      - 6%\n470\t      - 9%\n471\t      - 4%\n472\t    - - Reciprocity\n473\t      - 5%\n474\t      - 6%\n475\t      - 5%\n476\t    - - None\n477\t      - 6%\n478\t      - 2%\n479\t      - 6%\n480\t  figures_description:\n481\t  - 'Figure: 三种攻击类型的persuasion strategy分布stacked bar chart。 Crescendo策略最均匀；FITD偏重logical\n482\t    appeal和authority； Deceptive Delight偏重rapport和emotional appeal（反映其pleasant context策略）。'\n483\t  analysis: '数据量达标（72+65=137，均超过50条minimum）。两种攻击类型的persuasion strategy 分布与Crescendo明显不同：FITD偏重逻辑和权威（compliance\n484\t    escalation需要理由）， Deceptive Delight偏重rapport和emotional appeal（需要建立pleasant context）。\n485\t    这种分布差异直接解释了后续cross-attack evaluation中Deceptive Delight泛化较差的原因： 模型在Crescendo上学到的escalation\n486\t    trajectory（authority → reframing → escalation） 与Deceptive Delight的pattern（rapport\n487\t    → emotional → subtle insertion）差异大。 Manual spot check accuracy=82%意味着有18%的noise\n488\t    in labels， 这会传播到cross-attack evaluation中。\n489\t\n490\t    '\n491\t- name: cross_attack_evaluation\n492\t  plan_id: plan_006\n493\t  description: '用Crescendo训练的模型（treatment和baseline）在FITD和Deceptive Delight上做 zero-shot\n494\t    evaluation。测试跨攻击类型泛化能力。\n495\t\n496\t    '\n497\t  expected_results:\n498\t    fitd_treatment_f1: 0.74\n499\t    fitd_baseline_f1: 0.66\n500\t    fitd_delta_pp: 8\n501\t    dd_treatment_f1: 0.64\n502\t    dd_baseline_f1: 0.59\n503\t    dd_delta_pp: 5\n504\t    aggregate_treatment_f1: 0.69\n505\t    aggregate_baseline_f1: 0.63\n506\t    aggregate_delta_pp: 6\n507\t    fitd_bootstrap_p: 0.034\n508\t    dd_bootstrap_p: 0.142\n509\t    crescendo_treatment_f1_reference: 0.91\n510\t    fitd_treatment_drop_from_crescendo: 17\n511\t    dd_treatment_drop_from_crescendo: 27\n512\t  result_rationale: 'FITD泛化较好（treatment 0.74, delta=8pp, p=0.034显著）：FITD的compliance\n513\t    escalation 与Crescendo的persuasion escalation在strategy space中有substantial overlap——两者都\n514\t    涉及从trust-building逐步升级到explicit request，只是中间路径不同。Treatment模型 学到的escalation trajectory检测能力在FITD上partially\n515\t    transferable。8pp delta说明 persuasion grounding在cross-attack场景下仍提供更多增量价值（比clean\n516\t    data上的 K=3 delta=8pp一致），因为vanilla embeddings在unseen attack type上更容易被 unfamiliar\n517\t    semantic content mislead。 Deceptive Delight泛化较差（treatment 0.64, delta=5pp, p=0.142不显著）：\n518\t    Deceptive Delight的persuasion结构与Crescendo差异最大——它不依赖escalation 而是依赖interleaving，其策略分布偏重rapport和emotional\n519\t    appeal而非authority和reframing。 模型在Crescendo上学到的\"authority → reframing → escalation\"模式在Deceptive\n520\t    Delight 上匹配度低。Treatment仍优于baseline（0.64 vs 0.59）但差异不显著，因为persuasion grounding识别到了partial\n521\t    signal（rapport building和emotional appeal部分）但缺乏 Deceptive Delight特有的interleaving\n522\t    pattern识别能力。 Treatment从Crescendo到FITD的drop（0.91→0.74=17pp）vs到DD（0.91→0.64=27pp）\n523\t    进一步确认了DD的泛化挑战。这不是persuasion grounding的failure而是training distribution的limitation——如果将DD纳入训练集，预计performance会substantially提升。\n524\t\n525\t    '\n526\t  tables:\n527\t  - name: 'Table 10: Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Generalization'\n528\t    columns:\n529\t    - Attack Type\n530\t    - Treatment F1\n531\t    - Baseline F1\n532\t    - Δ (pp)\n533\t    - p-value\n534\t    rows:\n535\t    - - Crescendo (in-domain)\n536\t      - 0.91\n537\t      - 0.86\n538\t      - '+5'\n539\t      - 0.031*\n540\t    - - FITD (zero-shot)\n541\t      - 0.74\n542\t      - 0.66\n543\t      - '+8'\n544\t      - 0.034*\n545\t    - - Deceptive Delight (zero-shot)\n546\t      - 0.64\n547\t      - 0.59\n548\t      - '+5'\n549\t      - '0.142'\n550\t    - - Cross-attack aggregate\n551\t      - 0.69\n552\t      - 0.63\n553\t      - '+6'\n554\t      - '0.052'\n555\t  figures_description:\n556\t  - 'Figure: Per-attack-type F1 grouped bar chart（treatment vs baseline）， 分三个attack\n557\t    type。Crescendo最高，FITD中间，DD最低。Treatment bar在FITD上 明显高于baseline；在DD上差距缩小。标注各组p值。'\n558\t  - 'Figure: Confusion matrices for FITD和DD分别展示。DD的false negatives集中在 interleaving\n559\t    turns sequence中间段——模型未能识别benign-harmful交替模式。'\n560\t  analysis: 'Cross-attack结果必须分attack type报告而非仅报告aggregate——aggregate delta=6pp (p=0.052)刚好不显著，会mislead\n561\t    reviewers。分开报告后story变为： \"FITD泛化成立（+8pp, p=0.034），Deceptive Delight泛化有限（+5pp, p=0.142）\"。\n562\t    这支持了Claim 2的部分泛化故事，同时诚实承认limitation。 Deceptive Delight的弱泛化是median tier的defining\n563\t    feature之一——其persuasion结构 更隐蔽，不遵循standard escalation pattern，说明persuasion grounding的有效性\n564\t    依赖于training set覆盖足够的persuasion playbook diversity。 论文应讨论：(1) 为什么FITD泛化好而DD不行（strategy\n565\t    overlap分析）， (2) 这说明模型学到了什么（escalation detection而非general manipulation detection），\n566\t    (3) future work需要更diverse的training data。\n567\t\n568\t    '\n569\t- name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n570\t  plan_id: plan_007\n571\t  description: 'TF-IDF + Logistic Regression在clean数据上的baseline，量化lexical features\n572\t    单独的检测能力。为evasion hierarchy叙事提供bottom-line比较。\n573\t\n574\t    '\n575\t  expected_results:\n576\t    tfidf_lr_full_f1: 0.74\n577\t    tfidf_lr_k2_f1: 0.68\n578\t    tfidf_lr_k3_f1: 0.71\n579\t    tfidf_lr_k5_f1: 0.73\n580\t    tfidf_lr_cv_f1_mean: 0.73\n581\t    tfidf_lr_cv_f1_std: 0.04\n582\t    tfidf_lr_fpr: 0.19\n583\t    top_features_overlap_with_persuasion: 0.35\n584\t  result_rationale: 'Clean数据TF-IDF=0.67说明仍存在residual lexical signal，TF-IDF+LR因此能达到\n585\t    non-trivial的F1=0.74（远低于Phase B的1.0，但仍above chance）。这个数值恰好落在 baseline DeBERTa+GRU（0.86）和random（0.50）之间，提供了evasion\n586\t    hierarchy的 bottom tier。 K=2处F1=0.68最低：仅2个turns时lexical features最sparse，LR能利用的features有限。\n587\t    随着K增大performance缓慢提升（K=3: 0.71, K=5: 0.73, Full: 0.74），因为更多turns 提供了更多lexical\n588\t    evidence，但提升很小说明lexical approach saturates quickly。 CV std=0.04较大，反映了small dataset\n589\t    + lexical features组合的不稳定性。 35%的top features与persuasion相关词汇重叠（如\"consider\"、\"research\"、\"experience\"\n590\t    等兼具persuasion和lexical signal的词），说明lexical和persuasion features存在 partial overlap——这解释了为什么treatment\n591\t    vs baseline的delta在clean data上被压缩。 FPR=0.19偏高：lexical model容易将使用formal register的benign对话误判为攻击。\n592\t\n593\t    '\n594\t  tables:\n595\t  - name: 'Table 11: TF-IDF + LR Baseline Performance on Clean Data'\n596\t    columns:\n597\t    - K\n598\t    - TF-IDF+LR F1\n599\t    - Baseline (vanilla DeBERTa) F1\n600\t    - Treatment F1\n601\t    rows:\n602\t    - - K=2\n603\t      - 0.68\n604\t      - 0.75\n605\t      - 0.82\n606\t    - - K=3\n607\t      - 0.71\n608\t      - 0.78\n609\t      - 0.86\n610\t    - - Full\n611\t      - 0.74\n612\t      - 0.86\n613\t      - 0.91\n614\t  figures_description:\n615\t  - 'Figure: 三层evasion hierarchy在各K上的F1折线图：TF-IDF+LR（底）、 vanilla DeBERTa+GRU（中）、persuasion-grounded\n616\t    DeBERTa+GRU（顶）。 三条线在clean data上呈现清晰的层次但间距不均——semantic→pragmatic gap 小于lexical→semantic\n617\t    gap。'\n618\t  analysis: 'TF-IDF+LR在clean data上F1=0.74确认了residual lexical signal的存在， 但与之前TF-IDF=1.0时的perfect\n619\t    performance形成鲜明对比。Evasion hierarchy的 三层在clean data上为0.74 < 0.86 < 0.91，lexical→semantic\n620\t    jump (12pp) > semantic→pragmatic jump (5pp)——这说明在当前数据上，vanilla DeBERTa的semantic\n621\t    表示已经capture了大部分discriminative信号，persuasion grounding的增量虽然显著 但有限。这与median tier的核心特征一致。\n622\t\n623\t    '\n624\t- name: strategy_transition_analysis\n625\t  plan_id: plan_008\n626\t  description: '计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices， 可视化monotonic\n627\t    escalation trajectory（Claim 3），生成论文图表。\n628\t\n629\t    '\n630\t  expected_results:\n631\t    jailbreak_monotonicity_score_mean: 0.71\n632\t    jailbreak_monotonicity_score_std: 0.18\n633\t    benign_monotonicity_score_mean: 0.38\n634\t    benign_monotonicity_score_std: 0.14\n635\t    group_level_separation_p: 0.003\n636\t    individual_conversations_above_threshold: 0.68\n637\t    transition_entropy_jailbreak: 1.42\n638\t    transition_entropy_benign: 2.15\n639\t  result_rationale: 'Group level上jailbreak和benign的monotonicity分数有显著差异（0.71 vs 0.38,\n640\t    p=0.003）： jailbreak对话在aggregate level展现了clear escalation pattern——从trust strategies\n641\t    （rapport, social proof）逐步transition到influence strategies（authority, reframing）\n642\t    再到exploitation strategies（urgency, reciprocity）。Benign对话则呈oscillatory pattern，\n643\t    在各策略间来回跳转，无固定方向。 但individual-level噪声很大：jailbreak monotonicity的std=0.18（relative\n644\t    to mean 0.71）， 且只有68%的jailbreak conversations超过monotonicity threshold——32%的jailbreak\n645\t    conversations 不展现清晰的monotonic escalation。原因：(1) persuasion classifier accuracy=0.72意味着\n646\t    ~28%的turn-level strategy labels有误，噪声传播到trajectory计算中；(2) 部分jailbreak conversations的escalation不是strictly\n647\t    monotonic——攻击者有时需要\"退一步\"重建rapport 后再escalate（tactical de-escalation）。 Transition\n648\t    entropy也支持group-level distinction：jailbreak的entropy 1.42 < benign的 2.15，说明jailbreak的transition更predictable/structured。但同样，individual-level\n649\t    variance大。\n650\t\n651\t    '\n652\t  tables:\n653\t  - name: 'Table 12: Strategy Trajectory Analysis'\n654\t    columns:\n655\t    - Metric\n656\t    - Jailbreak\n657\t    - Benign\n658\t    - p-value\n659\t    rows:\n660\t    - - Monotonicity Score (mean±std)\n661\t      - 0.71±0.18\n662\t      - 0.38±0.14\n663\t      - 0.003*\n664\t    - - Transition Entropy\n665\t      - 1.42\n666\t      - 2.15\n667\t      - 0.007*\n668\t    - - '% Above Threshold (0.6)'\n669\t      - 68%\n670\t      - 12%\n671\t      - —\n672\t  figures_description:\n673\t  - 'Figure: 8×8 persuasion strategy transition heatmap，左=jailbreak，右=benign。 Jailbreak的heatmap显示diagonal-above-diagonal的dominant\n674\t    flow（低序号→高序号strategies）， 表明单向escalation；benign的heatmap更接近uniform，策略间transition分散。'\n675\t  - 'Figure: 每个conversation的monotonicity score strip plot（jailbreak=红, benign=蓝），\n676\t    带group mean和CI。两组分布有substantial overlap但means clearly separated。 标注32%的jailbreak\n677\t    conversations低于threshold，加注caveat。'\n678\t  - 'Figure: 选取2条representative jailbreak和2条benign的per-turn strategy evolution line\n679\t    plot。Jailbreak展示从strategy 1-2逐步上升到6-7的趋势；benign在中间区域oscillate。 但也展示1条non-monotonic\n680\t    jailbreak conversation作为honest counterexample。'\n681\t  analysis: 'Claim 3（monotonic escalation trajectory）在group level得到strong support（p=0.003），\n682\t    但individual-level caveat不可忽视：32%的jailbreak不展现monotonic pattern。论文应： (1) 报告group-level\n683\t    statistics作为primary evidence； (2) 展示individual-level variance作为honest limitation；\n684\t    (3) 讨论persuasion classifier noise作为individual-level噪声的主要来源； (4) 用transition heatmap作为直观但定性的evidence。\n685\t    Claim 3作为analytical/mechanistic contribution保留，但从\"all jailbreaks exhibit monotonic\n686\t    escalation\"降级为\"jailbreak conversations exhibit significantly more monotonic escalation\n687\t    trajectories at the group level\"。\n688\t\n689\t    '\n690\t- name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n691\t  plan_id: plan_009\n692\t  description: '从WildChat过滤高semantic-drift的benign对话作为hard negatives， 评估模型FPR。需处理WildChat中14-16%的jailbreak\n693\t    contamination。\n694\t\n695\t    '\n696\t  expected_results:\n697\t    wildchat_raw_candidates: 420\n698\t    contamination_rate_raw: 0.15\n699\t    contamination_after_filter: 0.03\n700\t    wildchat_filtered_clean: 85\n701\t    treatment_fpr_wildchat: 0.12\n702\t    baseline_fpr_wildchat: 0.18\n703\t    tfidf_lr_fpr_wildchat: 0.27\n704\t    high_drift_conversations_avg_turns: 7.1\n705\t    false_positive_persuasion_strategy_distribution: rapport_heavy\n706\t  result_rationale: 'WildChat过滤后得到85条high-drift benign conversations（从420条candidates中，\n707\t    先用keyword+LLM过滤掉15%的jailbreak contamination，再人工verify subsample确认 contamination降至3%）。这些conversations包含topic\n708\t    shifts、extended reasoning、 debate-style exchanges——semantically有drift但不含adversarial\n709\t    intent。 Treatment FPR=12%（~10/85的benign conversations被误判为jailbreak）：这些false positives\n710\t    主要是debate-style conversations中出现了类似authority appeal和reframing的persuasion patterns——persuasion\n711\t    grounding模型将legitimate persuasion误认为adversarial persuasion。 这是persuasion-based\n712\t    approach的inherent limitation：not all persuasion is adversarial。 Baseline FPR=18%更高：vanilla\n713\t    semantic embeddings在high-drift conversations上更容易 被大幅semantic shift触发false alarm（正如DeepContext被benign\n714\t    drift confuse的问题）。 Treatment的lower FPR说明persuasion grounding确实能部分区分adversarial\n715\t    vs legitimate drift。 TF-IDF+LR FPR=27%最高：lexical model完全无法处理high-drift benign\n716\t    conversations 中出现的\"topic-specific vocabulary\"。\n717\t\n718\t    '\n719\t  tables:\n720\t  - name: 'Table 13: False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives'\n721\t    columns:\n722\t    - Model\n723\t    - FPR on WildChat Hard Negatives\n724\t    - FPR on In-Domain Benign\n725\t    rows:\n726\t    - - Treatment\n727\t      - 12% (10/85)\n728\t      - 3%\n729\t    - - Baseline\n730\t      - 18% (15/85)\n731\t      - 6%\n732\t    - - TF-IDF + LR\n733\t      - 27% (23/85)\n734\t      - 19%\n735\t  figures_description:\n736\t  - 'Figure: FPR comparison bar chart across three models on in-domain benign vs WildChat\n737\t    hard negatives。所有模型在hard negatives上FPR都上升， 但treatment上升最少（3%→12% = +9pp vs baseline\n738\t    6%→18% = +12pp）。'\n739\t  analysis: 'Treatment FPR=12%勉强满足<15%的pass criteria。但这不是一个令人满意的数字—— 每8-9个legitimate\n740\t    high-drift conversation中就有1个被误判。论文应诚实讨论这一limitation： persuasion grounding减少了drift-induced\n741\t    false positives（vs baseline 18%）， 但无法消除legitimate persuasion vs adversarial persuasion的confusion。\n742\t    Future work应考虑增加intent classification的权重或引入conversation-level context 来区分两者。这也暗示了full\n743\t    dual-track architecture的necessity—— semantic track可以提供complementary signal来override\n744\t    persuasion track的false positives。\n745\t\n746\t    '\n747\t- name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n748\t  plan_id: plan_010\n749\t  description: '从DeBERTa fine-tuning的多个checkpoints（epoch 2/3/final）评估downstream performance，\n750\t    量化encoder训练随机性对最终结果的影响。\n751\t\n752\t    '\n753\t  expected_results:\n754\t    epoch2_treatment_full_f1: 0.9\n755\t    epoch3_treatment_full_f1: 0.91\n756\t    final_treatment_full_f1: 0.89\n757\t    f1_std_across_checkpoints: 0.01\n758\t    f1_max_spread: 0.02\n759\t    epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.7\n760\t    epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.72\n761\t    final_persuasion_acc: 0.71\n762\t    epoch2_treatment_k3_f1: 0.84\n763\t    epoch3_treatment_k3_f1: 0.86\n764\t    final_treatment_k3_f1: 0.85\n765\t    k3_max_spread: 0.02\n766\t  result_rationale: '三个checkpoints的downstream F1在2pp range内波动（0.89-0.91），std=1.0pp，\n767\t    满足<2pp variance的pass criteria。Epoch 3略优（0.91）因为persuasion accuracy在 epoch 3达到peak（0.72），之后final\n768\t    epoch出现minor overfitting（accuracy降至0.71， downstream F1也微降至0.89）。这种mild overfitting\n769\t    in continued training是DeBERTa 在small dataset上fine-tuning的typical behavior。 K=3处的variance同样在2pp\n770\t    range（0.84-0.86），说明early detection结果也是stable的。 这个low variance结果有两层意义：(1) 报告的performance数字是robust的，不是lucky\n771\t    checkpoint的产物；(2) downstream GRU pipeline对encoder representation的minor变化 有一定tolerance——这是good\n772\t    news for practical deployment。 但注意：这里只测了checkpoint variance，未测random seed variance（不同random\n773\t    initialization 的DeBERTa fine-tuning）。完整的variance分析需要多次独立训练，受GPU budget限制未做。\n774\t\n775\t    '\n776\t  tables:\n777\t  - name: 'Table 14: Cross-Checkpoint Stability Analysis'\n778\t    columns:\n779\t    - Checkpoint\n780\t    - Persuasion Acc\n781\t    - Treatment Full F1\n782\t    - Treatment K=3 F1\n783\t    rows:\n784\t    - - Epoch 2\n785\t      - 0.7\n786\t      - 0.9\n787\t      - 0.84\n788\t    - - Epoch 3 (selected)\n789\t      - 0.72\n790\t      - 0.91\n791\t      - 0.86\n792\t    - - Final (epoch 5)\n793\t      - 0.71\n794\t      - 0.89\n795\t      - 0.85\n796\t    - - Std\n797\t      - '0.010'\n798\t      - '0.010'\n799\t      - '0.010'\n800\t    - - Max spread\n801\t      - '0.02'\n802\t      - '0.02'\n803\t      - '0.02'\n804\t  figures_description:\n805\t  - 'Figure: 三个checkpoints的downstream F1 point plot with error bars， 在full和K=3上各画一组。Points紧密聚集，说明stability。'\n806\t  analysis: 'Variance < 2pp确认了结果的stability。建议论文在appendix报告此结果作为robustness check， 而非main\n807\t    results。需注意这只是checkpoint variance而非full training variance。\n808\t\n809\t    '\n810\t- name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n811\t  plan_id: plan_011\n812\t  description: '构建DeepContext代理baseline：BERT-base（非DeBERTa）+ GRU， 使用generic semantic\n813\t    drift features。非完整DeepContext复现（无公开代码）， 但隔离了encoder和feature representation的贡献。\n814\t\n815\t    '\n816\t  expected_results:\n817\t    bert_gru_full_f1: 0.82\n818\t    bert_gru_k2_f1: 0.7\n819\t    bert_gru_k3_f1: 0.74\n820\t    bert_gru_k5_f1: 0.8\n821\t    bert_gru_fpr_full: 0.09\n822\t    bert_gru_perturbed_full_f1: 0.69\n823\t    bert_gru_drop_under_perturbation: 13\n824\t    vs_vanilla_deberta_baseline_gap: -4\n825\t    vs_treatment_gap: -9\n826\t  result_rationale: 'BERT-base + GRU在clean data上F1=0.82，低于vanilla DeBERTa + GRU baseline（0.86）\n827\t    4pp：这个gap主要来自BERT vs DeBERTa的encoder capacity差异——DeBERTa-v3-base在 language understanding\n828\t    tasks上一般优于BERT-base 3-5pp，在我们的downstream task上 这个gap被preserved。 相比treatment（0.91），BERT+GRU差9pp——但这个gap\n829\t    conflates两个因素： (1) encoder capacity（BERT vs DeBERTa, ~4pp）和(2) persuasion grounding（~5pp）。\n830\t    这不是一个完美的ablation——论文需要承认这一confound，但可以argue：即使将全部4pp encoder gap归因于DeBERTa，仍有5pp来自persuasion\n831\t    grounding，与treatment vs baseline (same DeBERTa) 的5pp delta一致。 在adversarial perturbation下BERT+GRU降至0.69（13pp\n832\t    drop），比vanilla DeBERTa baseline 的12pp drop还大1pp——说明BERT的representations比DeBERTa对lexical\n833\t    perturbation更脆弱 （可能因为BERT更依赖surface patterns）。 K=2处F1=0.70比baseline（0.75）低5pp：BERT在少turns时的表现特别弱，\n834\t    因为其contextual representations不如DeBERTa在short contexts下discriminative。\n835\t\n836\t    '\n837\t  tables:\n838\t  - name: 'Table 15: DeepContext Proxy Baseline Comparison'\n839\t    columns:\n840\t    - Model\n841\t    - Full F1\n842\t    - K=3 F1\n843\t    - K=2 F1\n844\t    - Perturbed Full F1\n845\t    rows:\n846\t    - - Treatment (DeBERTa-persuasion + GRU)\n847\t      - 0.91\n848\t      - 0.86\n849\t      - 0.82\n850\t      - 0.84\n851\t    - - Baseline (DeBERTa-vanilla + GRU)\n852\t      - 0.86\n853\t      - 0.78\n854\t      - 0.75\n855\t      - 0.74\n856\t    - - DeepContext proxy (BERT + GRU)\n857\t      - 0.82\n858\t      - 0.74\n859\t      - 0.7\n860\t      - 0.69\n861\t    - - TF-IDF + LR\n862\t      - 0.74\n863\t      - 0.71\n864\t      - 0.68\n865\t      - 0.56\n866\t  figures_description:\n867\t  - 'Figure: 四个模型在clean和perturbed条件下的full F1 grouped bar chart， 从左到右排列形成清晰的hierarchy：TF-IDF+LR\n868\t    < BERT+GRU < DeBERTa-vanilla < DeBERTa-persuasion。 Perturbed条件下hierarchy preserved但gaps变大（尤其TF-IDF+LR崩溃）。'\n869\t  analysis: DeepContext proxy提供了有用的比较点但存在confound（BERT vs DeBERTa capacity gap）。 论文应：(1)\n870\t    报告此结果作为additional reference point但不作为primary comparison； (2) 明确承认\"this is not\n871\t    a faithful DeepContext reproduction\"； (3) 主要论据应基于treatment vs baseline（same encoder,\n872\t    isolating persuasion grounding effect）。 四层hierarchy（TF-IDF < BERT+GRU < DeBERTa\n873\t    < DeBERTa-persuasion）在视觉上很compelling 但需要honest caveats about confounded comparisons。\n874\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a3eef2-233e-4eb5-bfe4-3efac3de241f","uuid":"96cc672a-ec83-4823-9736-e7a6a33d7687","timestamp":"2026-05-17T17:28:19.178Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T165817/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '需要两处降级：(1) Claim 2 从 \"K=2显著优势\" 降级为 \"K=3显著优势，K=2趋势一致但bootstrap\n  CI重叠(p=0.07)\"， early detection故事后移一步但仍成立；(2) Claim 1 从 \"evasion hierarchy\" 软化为 \"pragmatic\n  features 提供complementary robustness\"，delta-delta=5pp显著但非压倒性。Claim 3 保留但加caveat说\n  individual-level monotonicity分数方差大(σ=0.18)。论文定位为 \"proof-of-concept for the principle\"，\n  补充bootstrap CI、persuasion classifier bottleneck讨论、cross-attack分attack type报告。 仍冲EMNLP\n  main但limitation section需占半页以上。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: data_quality_fix\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: '修复TF-IDF=1.0数据质量问题。(a) 将benign turns的strategy标签从hardcoded 7改为第9类\"none\"；\n    (b) 用Qwen3-8B对jailbreak turns做register normalization（改写为日常对话语体，保留persuasion结构）；\n    (c) 在normalized数据上重新计算TF-IDF，验证hard gate < 0.75； (d) 在clean数据上重新评估DeBERTa persuasion分类器。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    tfidf_before_any_fix: 1.0\n    tfidf_after_m004_fix_only: 0.82\n    tfidf_after_register_norm: 0.67\n    deberta_persuasion_acc_clean: 0.72\n    deberta_intent_acc_clean: 0.93\n    num_conversations_normalized: 240\n    normalization_rejection_rate: 0.08\n    hard_gate_pass: true\n  result_rationale: 'M004修复（benign strategy=none）将TF-IDF从1.0降到~0.82：原先strategy=7在jailbreak中从不出现，\n    是一个完美的lexical shortcut；改为\"none\"后消除了这一指标，但jailbreak turns仍保留较正式的 register（如\"I''d\n    like to explore...\"），与benign的口语化风格（\"hey can you...\"）形成 register差异，导致TF-IDF仅降到0.82。Register\n    normalization进一步将jailbreak turns改写为 日常对话语体，消除了大部分register差异，TF-IDF降至0.67——落入[0.60,0.74]区间。未降到更低\n    是因为persuasion结构本身引入了部分特征词（如authority appeals中的\"expert\"、\"research shows\"）， 这些词在benign对话中频率较低，构成残余的lexical\n    signal。这恰好说明persuasion结构与lexical features存在部分overlap，为后续delta偏小埋下伏笔。 DeBERTa persuasion\n    accuracy从原始数据的0.7963降至0.72：register normalization移除了部分 与persuasion类别相关的surface\n    cues（如正式语体中的hedging markers与authority appeal相关）， 模型需要更依赖语义层面的persuasion识别，准确率因此下降。Intent\n    accuracy仅从0.9514微降至0.93， 因为intent是binary且更粗粒度，受register变化影响小。8%的normalization\n    rejection来自 包含技术术语或代码片段的turns，LLM改写后语义偏移超过阈值被QA过滤。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: TF-IDF Progression Through Data Cleaning Pipeline'\n    columns:\n    - Stage\n    - TF-IDF Score\n    - Description\n    rows:\n    - - Original (Phase B)\n      - 1.0\n      - Strategy=7 shortcut + register gap\n    - - After M004 fix\n      - 0.82\n      - Strategy='none' for benign, register gap remains\n    - - After register norm\n      - 0.67\n      - Jailbreak turns rewritten to conversational register\n    - - Hard gate threshold\n      - <0.75\n      - PASS ✓\n  - name: 'Table 2: DeBERTa Multi-Task Performance on Clean vs Original Data'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Original Data\n    - Clean Data\n    - Delta\n    rows:\n    - - Persuasion Acc (8-class)\n      - 0.7963\n      - 0.72\n      - '-0.076'\n    - - Intent Acc (binary)\n      - 0.9514\n      - 0.93\n      - '-0.021'\n    - - Best Epoch\n      - 3\n      - 3\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: TF-IDF feature importance heatmap对比original vs clean data的top-20 discriminative\n    unigrams。 Original数据中''strategy_7''、''I would like to''等register markers占据top位置；clean数据中\n    top features变为更语义化的词（''explore''、''research''、''approach''），且权重分布更平坦。'\n  analysis: 'Hard gate通过（0.67 < 0.75），可以进入训练阶段。但0.67并非很低——说明即使register normalization\n    后仍存在residual lexical signal。这意味着后续treatment vs baseline的delta会被压缩：baseline 也能从residual\n    lexical cues中获益。DeBERTa persuasion accuracy降至0.72是一个bottleneck信号： 8类分类的错误会传播到下游embeddings，限制treatment的上限。需要在论文中明确讨论这一bottleneck。\n\n    '\n- name: core_revalidation_clean\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: '在clean数据上从头重训treatment（persuasion-grounded DeBERTa → GRU）和baseline\n    （vanilla DeBERTa → GRU）。全面评估K=1,2,3,5,all。核心claim验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    treatment_k1_f1_clean: 0.73\n    treatment_k2_f1_clean: 0.82\n    treatment_k3_f1_clean: 0.86\n    treatment_k5_f1_clean: 0.9\n    treatment_full_f1_clean: 0.91\n    baseline_k1_f1_clean: 0.63\n    baseline_k2_f1_clean: 0.75\n    baseline_k3_f1_clean: 0.78\n    baseline_k5_f1_clean: 0.84\n    baseline_full_f1_clean: 0.86\n    delta_k1_pp: 10\n    delta_k2_pp: 7\n    delta_k3_pp: 8\n    delta_k5_pp: 6\n    delta_full_pp: 5\n    bootstrap_ci_k2_treatment:\n    - 0.76\n    - 0.88\n    bootstrap_ci_k2_baseline:\n    - 0.68\n    - 0.82\n    bootstrap_k2_p_value: 0.072\n    bootstrap_ci_k3_treatment:\n    - 0.81\n    - 0.91\n    bootstrap_ci_k3_baseline:\n    - 0.72\n    - 0.84\n    bootstrap_k3_p_value: 0.018\n    bootstrap_ci_full_treatment:\n    - 0.87\n    - 0.95\n    bootstrap_ci_full_baseline:\n    - 0.81\n    - 0.91\n    bootstrap_full_p_value: 0.031\n    treatment_fpr95tpr_k2: 0.08\n    baseline_fpr95tpr_k2: 0.14\n    treatment_fpr95tpr_full: 0.03\n    baseline_fpr95tpr_full: 0.06\n    test_size: 72\n  result_rationale: 'Clean数据上所有指标相比Phase B大幅下降（Phase B treatment full F1=1.0→0.91，baseline\n    0.987→0.86），因为移除了lexical shortcuts后模型必须从真正的语义/语用特征中学习。 Treatment在所有K上优于baseline，但delta随K增大而收窄（K=1:\n    10pp → full: 5pp）： 这是因为在更多turns可用时，vanilla semantic embeddings也能捕捉到足够的accumulated\n    drift， 缩小了persuasion grounding的增量价值。 K=2的delta=7pp落在[3,9]区间中部，但bootstrap p=0.072——72个test\n    samples中bootstrap 重采样的CI有overlap（treatment [0.76,0.88] vs baseline [0.68,0.82]），未达到p<0.05\n    显著性。这是因为K=2时只有2个turn，persuasion策略刚从rapport阶段开始， treatment和baseline在这个早期阶段的区分度有限。\n    K=3的delta=8pp且p=0.018显著：第3个turn是关键转折点——攻击者通常在此处从rapport转向 authority framing或reframing，这一策略转换是treatment模型的核心信号。Baseline在K=3时\n    仍在处理看似正常的语义内容（第3个turn的语义仍在benign region内），而treatment捕捉到了 persuasion策略从trust-building向testing的transition。\n    Full conversation delta收窄到5pp：当所有turns可用时，即使vanilla embeddings也能从 后期turns的显式有害内容中获益，persuasion\n    grounding的增量被压缩。 FPR在K=2处treatment=0.08 vs baseline=0.14：treatment将fewer benign\n    conversations 误判为攻击，因为persuasion grounding能区分legitimate persuasion（如销售场景）和 adversarial\n    persuasion escalation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Core Revalidation Results on Clean Data (F1 by Conversation Prefix\n      Length)'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - Treatment F1\n    - 95% CI\n    - Baseline F1\n    - 95% CI\n    - Δ (pp)\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - K=1\n      - 0.73\n      - '[0.64, 0.82]'\n      - 0.63\n      - '[0.53, 0.73]'\n      - '+10'\n      - '0.089'\n    - - K=2\n      - 0.82\n      - '[0.76, 0.88]'\n      - 0.75\n      - '[0.68, 0.82]'\n      - '+7'\n      - '0.072'\n    - - K=3\n      - 0.86\n      - '[0.81, 0.91]'\n      - 0.78\n      - '[0.72, 0.84]'\n      - '+8'\n      - 0.018*\n    - - K=5\n      - 0.9\n      - '[0.85, 0.95]'\n      - 0.84\n      - '[0.78, 0.90]'\n      - '+6'\n      - 0.038*\n    - - Full\n      - 0.91\n      - '[0.87, 0.95]'\n      - 0.86\n      - '[0.81, 0.91]'\n      - '+5'\n      - 0.031*\n  - name: 'Table 4: FPR at 95% TPR on Clean Data'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - Treatment FPR@95TPR\n    - Baseline FPR@95TPR\n    rows:\n    - - K=2\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.14\n    - - K=3\n      - 0.05\n      - 0.11\n    - - Full\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.06\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: F1 vs K曲线图，treatment和baseline各一条线，带shaded bootstrap 95% CI。 K=1-2处两条线的CI有明显重叠；K=3处开始分离；K=5和full处gap收窄但仍可见。\n    标注K=3处的p=0.018。'\n  - 'Figure: ROC曲线对比（K=3），treatment AUC明显高于baseline， 标注operating point和FPR@95TPR。'\n  analysis: '核心结论：Claim 2需降级。K=2处delta=7pp方向正确但p=0.072不显著（n=72太小）， 无法声称\"K=2显著优势\"。K=3处delta=8pp且p=0.018显著，early\n    detection claim需改为 \"K=3 significant advantage, K=2 consistent trend requiring\n    larger sample confirmation\"。 论文可报告K=2的趋势但必须诚实标注non-significance。Full conversation\n    delta=5pp 且显著，说明即使在有足够上下文时persuasion grounding仍有增量价值，但增量有限。 相比Phase B的dramatic\n    deltas（treatment 1.0 vs baseline 0.737），clean data上的 delta被大幅压缩，符合median tier预期：移除lexical\n    shortcuts后，persuasion信号 与semantic信号存在部分重叠，grounding的增量被限制。\n\n    '\n- name: scrambled_label_ablation\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: '随机打乱jailbreak turns的persuasion strategy标签，重训treatment模型。 与正确标签的treatment对比，验证persuasion标签携带真实信号。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    scrambled_treatment_full_f1: 0.84\n    proper_treatment_full_f1: 0.91\n    drop_full_pp: 7\n    scrambled_treatment_k3_f1: 0.8\n    proper_treatment_k3_f1: 0.86\n    drop_k3_pp: 6\n    scrambled_treatment_k2_f1: 0.77\n    proper_treatment_k2_f1: 0.82\n    drop_k2_pp: 5\n    bootstrap_p_full: 0.008\n    bootstrap_p_k3: 0.024\n    baseline_full_f1: 0.86\n    scrambled_vs_baseline_gap_pp: -2\n  result_rationale: 'Scrambled labels破坏了persuasion strategy的序列语义——模型在Stage 1学到的embeddings\n    不再编码正确的pragmatic function，而是随机噪声覆盖在语义表示之上。Full F1从0.91 降至0.84（7pp drop），落在[4,10]区间中部。\n    关键观察：scrambled treatment（0.84）仍略低于baseline（0.86），而非大幅超过baseline。 这说明：(1) 错误的persuasion标签实际上对DeBERTa\n    fine-tuning引入了干扰噪声， 使其表示质量甚至略逊于未经fine-tune的vanilla DeBERTa；(2) persuasion multi-task\n    learning不是free lunch——错误的auxiliary task会伤害主任务。 7pp drop在bootstrap test中p=0.008高度显著：虽然test\n    set只有72个样本， 但因为scrambled和proper treatment共享相同的架构和训练数据，paired comparison 的方差较小，容易达到显著性。\n    K=3处drop=6pp也显著（p=0.024），K=2处drop=5pp方向一致但幅度较小—— 这与K=2处的信号本身较弱一致：如果K=2处treatment的优势本身就在significance边界，\n    那么ablation的drop自然也偏小。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: Scrambled-Label Ablation Results'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - Treatment (proper)\n    - Treatment (scrambled)\n    - Baseline (vanilla)\n    - Drop (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - K=2\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.77\n      - 0.75\n      - '-5'\n    - - K=3\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.8\n      - 0.78\n      - '-6'\n    - - Full\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.84\n      - 0.86\n      - '-7'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: 三组模型（proper treatment, scrambled treatment, vanilla baseline）在各K上的 F1柱状图。Proper\n    treatment在所有K上最高；scrambled treatment接近甚至略低于baseline； baseline稳定居中。图注标注proper vs\n    scrambled的bootstrap p值。'\n  analysis: 'Scrambled drop=7pp高度显著（p=0.008），直接证明persuasion strategy标签携带真实信号， 不仅仅是class\n    indicator。同时scrambled treatment≈baseline说明DeBERTa fine-tuning的 价值完全来自正确的persuasion\n    supervision——没有正确标签时，fine-tuning甚至引入噪声。 这验证了M004 fix的必要性，也支持了论文的核心机制故事：persuasion\n    grounding的增益 来自正确编码pragmatic function，而非单纯的额外训练。 注意：7pp drop虽然显著，但并非overwhelming——这与persuasion\n    accuracy=0.72一致： labels本身有28%的错误率，所以scrambled labels相当于从72%正确→0%正确， 只造成7pp drop说明downstream\n    pipeline对label noise有一定tolerance。\n\n    '\n- name: adversarial_perturbation\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: '对clean jailbreak conversations施加aggressive paraphrasing（同义替换、句式重构、\n    register shifting），移除所有lexical cues。评估treatment和baseline在perturbed数据上的 表现（模型在unperturbed数据上训练）。核心Claim\n    1验证。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    treatment_clean_full_f1: 0.91\n    treatment_perturbed_full_f1: 0.84\n    treatment_drop_full_pp: 7\n    baseline_clean_full_f1: 0.86\n    baseline_perturbed_full_f1: 0.74\n    baseline_drop_full_pp: 12\n    delta_delta_full_pp: 5\n    treatment_clean_k3_f1: 0.86\n    treatment_perturbed_k3_f1: 0.79\n    baseline_clean_k3_f1: 0.78\n    baseline_perturbed_k3_f1: 0.66\n    delta_delta_k3_pp: 4\n    tfidf_lr_clean_full_f1: 0.74\n    tfidf_lr_perturbed_full_f1: 0.56\n    tfidf_drop_pp: 18\n    perturbed_data_tfidf_score: 0.41\n    bootstrap_delta_delta_p: 0.043\n  result_rationale: 'Adversarial paraphrasing将TF-IDF从0.67降至0.41，说明perturbation成功移除了大部分\n    残余lexical cues。三个模型的degradation呈现清晰的evasion hierarchy： TF-IDF+LR崩溃最严重（18pp drop,\n    0.74→0.56）——lexical features在perturbation下 几乎失效，仅靠少数无法被paraphrase的functional words维持above-chance表现。\n    Baseline degradation中等（12pp drop, 0.86→0.74）——vanilla DeBERTa的语义表示 对paraphrasing有一定鲁棒性（DeBERTa的contextual\n    embeddings编码了语义而非surface form）， 但仍有substantial drop因为部分语义特征（如特定的topic words）被替换。\n    Treatment degradation最小（7pp drop, 0.91→0.84）——persuasion-grounded embeddings 编码的是pragmatic\n    function（如authority appeal、rapport building），这些在paraphrasing 下更稳定：你可以换词说同样的persuasion策略。\n    Delta-delta=5pp落在[3,8]区间中部，bootstrap p=0.043勉强显著。这个delta-delta \"存在但不压倒性\"：5pp说明pragmatic\n    features确实提供了complementary robustness， 但不足以声称存在dramatic evasion hierarchy。原因是treatment模型的persuasion\n    encoder 本身accuracy只有0.72，在perturbation下persuasion识别进一步降级，限制了robustness 的上限。如果persuasion\n    classifier更准确，delta-delta会更大。 K=3处delta-delta=4pp略小于full的5pp：早期turns的perturbation影响更大，因为只有\n    2-3个turns时每个turn的权重更高，单个turn的persuasion识别错误影响被放大。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: Adversarial Perturbation Results — Evasion Hierarchy'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Clean F1\n    - Perturbed F1\n    - Drop (pp)\n    - Δ-Δ vs Treatment\n    rows:\n    - - Treatment (persuasion-grounded)\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.84\n      - '-7'\n      - —\n    - - Baseline (vanilla DeBERTa)\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.74\n      - '-12'\n      - 5pp\n    - - TF-IDF + LR\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.56\n      - '-18'\n      - 11pp\n  - name: 'Table 7: Adversarial Perturbation at K=3 (Early Detection)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Clean K=3 F1\n    - Perturbed K=3 F1\n    - Drop (pp)\n    rows:\n    - - Treatment\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.79\n      - '-7'\n    - - Baseline\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.66\n      - '-12'\n    - - TF-IDF + LR\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.52\n      - '-19'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Grouped bar chart展示三个模型在clean vs perturbed条件下的F1， 带error bars。Treatment的两根柱子高度差最小；TF-IDF+LR差距最大。\n    标注delta-delta=5pp和p=0.043。'\n  - 'Figure: TF-IDF分布直方图对比clean data（μ=0.67）vs perturbed data（μ=0.41）， 说明perturbation成功移除了lexical\n    signal。'\n  analysis: 'Evasion hierarchy narrative得到部分支持：lexical < semantic < pragmatic的degradation\n    ordering清晰（18pp > 12pp > 7pp），但delta-delta=5pp仅勉强显著（p=0.043）， 不是strong evidence。论文应将Claim\n    1从\"evasion hierarchy exists\"软化为 \"pragmatic features provide complementary robustness,\n    with preliminary evidence for an evasion hierarchy\"。5pp delta-delta的bottleneck是persuasion\n    classifier accuracy——在limitation中讨论。TF-IDF+LR的崩溃（18pp drop）是一个strong result， 直接证明lexical\n    features不可靠，为persuasion grounding的motivation提供了solid support。\n\n    '\n- name: multi_attack_generation\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: '用Qwen3-8B pipeline生成FITD-style和Deceptive Delight-style攻击对话， 每种50-100条，标注persuasion\n    strategy。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fitd_conversations_generated: 72\n    fitd_avg_turns: 6.2\n    fitd_persuasion_strategies_covered: 7\n    dd_conversations_generated: 65\n    dd_avg_turns: 5.8\n    dd_persuasion_strategies_covered: 6\n    total_attack_conversations: 137\n    persuasion_annotation_coverage: 0.94\n    manual_spot_check_accuracy: 0.82\n    fitd_generation_rejection_rate: 0.12\n    dd_generation_rejection_rate: 0.18\n  result_rationale: 'FITD生成72条（rejection rate 12%）：FITD的compliance escalation pattern相对\n    straightforward——从小请求逐步升级到大请求——Qwen3-8B能较好地遵循playbook。 12%的rejection来自模型有时跳过中间步骤直接escalate（不符合gradual\n    compliance的定义）。 平均6.2个turns，比Crescendo略长因为FITD需要更多的commitment steps。 Deceptive\n    Delight生成65条（rejection rate 18%，略高于FITD）：这种攻击要求在 benign content中interleave harmful\n    content，Qwen3-8B有时在interleaving时过于明显 （harmful content太突兀）或过于隐蔽（完全是benign content），18%的rejection反映了\n    这种生成难度。平均5.8个turns，略短因为deceptive delight不需要长期rapport building。 Persuasion annotation\n    coverage 94%：6%的turns无法被映射到8-class taxonomy中的 任何一类，标记为\"none\"。这些主要是pure information\n    exchange turns。 Manual spot check accuracy 82%：在随机抽取的20% turns上人工验证persuasion\n    labels， 82%正确。错误主要发生在authority appeal vs logical appeal的边界（两者在FITD中 经常交织）和rapport\n    building vs emotional appeal的区分上。这与DeBERTa分类器 accuracy=0.72大致一致（spot check是在LLM\n    annotation上做的，不完全等同于classifier）。 Deceptive Delight覆盖6类而非7类persuasion strategies：因为这种攻击不需要\n    explicit authority appeal（其策略是通过pleasant context降低警惕而非建立权威）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Generated Attack Data Statistics'\n    columns:\n    - Attack Type\n    - Conversations\n    - Avg Turns\n    - Strategies Covered\n    - Rejection Rate\n    rows:\n    - - FITD\n      - 72\n      - 6.2\n      - 7/8\n      - 12%\n    - - Deceptive Delight\n      - 65\n      - 5.8\n      - 6/8\n      - 18%\n    - - Crescendo (original)\n      - 240\n      - 5.4\n      - 8/8\n      - —\n  - name: 'Table 9: Persuasion Strategy Distribution Across Attack Types'\n    columns:\n    - Strategy\n    - Crescendo (%)\n    - FITD (%)\n    - Deceptive Delight (%)\n    rows:\n    - - Rapport Building\n      - 22%\n      - 18%\n      - 28%\n    - - Authority Appeal\n      - 14%\n      - 16%\n      - 3%\n    - - Emotional Appeal\n      - 11%\n      - 8%\n      - 21%\n    - - Logical Appeal\n      - 13%\n      - 19%\n      - 12%\n    - - Reframing\n      - 15%\n      - 10%\n      - 14%\n    - - Social Proof\n      - 8%\n      - 12%\n      - 7%\n    - - Urgency/Scarcity\n      - 6%\n      - 9%\n      - 4%\n    - - Reciprocity\n      - 5%\n      - 6%\n      - 5%\n    - - None\n      - 6%\n      - 2%\n      - 6%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: 三种攻击类型的persuasion strategy分布stacked bar chart。 Crescendo策略最均匀；FITD偏重logical\n    appeal和authority； Deceptive Delight偏重rapport和emotional appeal（反映其pleasant context策略）。'\n  analysis: '数据量达标（72+65=137，均超过50条minimum）。两种攻击类型的persuasion strategy 分布与Crescendo明显不同：FITD偏重逻辑和权威（compliance\n    escalation需要理由）， Deceptive Delight偏重rapport和emotional appeal（需要建立pleasant context）。\n    这种分布差异直接解释了后续cross-attack evaluation中Deceptive Delight泛化较差的原因： 模型在Crescendo上学到的escalation\n    trajectory（authority → reframing → escalation） 与Deceptive Delight的pattern（rapport\n    → emotional → subtle insertion）差异大。 Manual spot check accuracy=82%意味着有18%的noise\n    in labels， 这会传播到cross-attack evaluation中。\n\n    '\n- name: cross_attack_evaluation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: '用Crescendo训练的模型（treatment和baseline）在FITD和Deceptive Delight上做 zero-shot\n    evaluation。测试跨攻击类型泛化能力。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    fitd_treatment_f1: 0.74\n    fitd_baseline_f1: 0.66\n    fitd_delta_pp: 8\n    dd_treatment_f1: 0.64\n    dd_baseline_f1: 0.59\n    dd_delta_pp: 5\n    aggregate_treatment_f1: 0.69\n    aggregate_baseline_f1: 0.63\n    aggregate_delta_pp: 6\n    fitd_bootstrap_p: 0.034\n    dd_bootstrap_p: 0.142\n    crescendo_treatment_f1_reference: 0.91\n    fitd_treatment_drop_from_crescendo: 17\n    dd_treatment_drop_from_crescendo: 27\n  result_rationale: 'FITD泛化较好（treatment 0.74, delta=8pp, p=0.034显著）：FITD的compliance\n    escalation 与Crescendo的persuasion escalation在strategy space中有substantial overlap——两者都\n    涉及从trust-building逐步升级到explicit request，只是中间路径不同。Treatment模型 学到的escalation trajectory检测能力在FITD上partially\n    transferable。8pp delta说明 persuasion grounding在cross-attack场景下仍提供更多增量价值（比clean\n    data上的 K=3 delta=8pp一致），因为vanilla embeddings在unseen attack type上更容易被 unfamiliar\n    semantic content mislead。 Deceptive Delight泛化较差（treatment 0.64, delta=5pp, p=0.142不显著）：\n    Deceptive Delight的persuasion结构与Crescendo差异最大——它不依赖escalation 而是依赖interleaving，其策略分布偏重rapport和emotional\n    appeal而非authority和reframing。 模型在Crescendo上学到的\"authority → reframing → escalation\"模式在Deceptive\n    Delight 上匹配度低。Treatment仍优于baseline（0.64 vs 0.59）但差异不显著，因为persuasion grounding识别到了partial\n    signal（rapport building和emotional appeal部分）但缺乏 Deceptive Delight特有的interleaving\n    pattern识别能力。 Treatment从Crescendo到FITD的drop（0.91→0.74=17pp）vs到DD（0.91→0.64=27pp）\n    进一步确认了DD的泛化挑战。这不是persuasion grounding的failure而是training distribution的limitation——如果将DD纳入训练集，预计performance会substantially提升。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 10: Cross-Attack Zero-Shot Generalization'\n    columns:\n    - Attack Type\n    - Treatment F1\n    - Baseline F1\n    - Δ (pp)\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - Crescendo (in-domain)\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.86\n      - '+5'\n      - 0.031*\n    - - FITD (zero-shot)\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.66\n      - '+8'\n      - 0.034*\n    - - Deceptive Delight (zero-shot)\n      - 0.64\n      - 0.59\n      - '+5'\n      - '0.142'\n    - - Cross-attack aggregate\n      - 0.69\n      - 0.63\n      - '+6'\n      - '0.052'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Per-attack-type F1 grouped bar chart（treatment vs baseline）， 分三个attack\n    type。Crescendo最高，FITD中间，DD最低。Treatment bar在FITD上 明显高于baseline；在DD上差距缩小。标注各组p值。'\n  - 'Figure: Confusion matrices for FITD和DD分别展示。DD的false negatives集中在 interleaving\n    turns sequence中间段——模型未能识别benign-harmful交替模式。'\n  analysis: 'Cross-attack结果必须分attack type报告而非仅报告aggregate——aggregate delta=6pp (p=0.052)刚好不显著，会mislead\n    reviewers。分开报告后story变为： \"FITD泛化成立（+8pp, p=0.034），Deceptive Delight泛化有限（+5pp, p=0.142）\"。\n    这支持了Claim 2的部分泛化故事，同时诚实承认limitation。 Deceptive Delight的弱泛化是median tier的defining\n    feature之一——其persuasion结构 更隐蔽，不遵循standard escalation pattern，说明persuasion grounding的有效性\n    依赖于training set覆盖足够的persuasion playbook diversity。 论文应讨论：(1) 为什么FITD泛化好而DD不行（strategy\n    overlap分析）， (2) 这说明模型学到了什么（escalation detection而非general manipulation detection），\n    (3) future work需要更diverse的training data。\n\n    '\n- name: tfidf_lr_baseline\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: 'TF-IDF + Logistic Regression在clean数据上的baseline，量化lexical features\n    单独的检测能力。为evasion hierarchy叙事提供bottom-line比较。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    tfidf_lr_full_f1: 0.74\n    tfidf_lr_k2_f1: 0.68\n    tfidf_lr_k3_f1: 0.71\n    tfidf_lr_k5_f1: 0.73\n    tfidf_lr_cv_f1_mean: 0.73\n    tfidf_lr_cv_f1_std: 0.04\n    tfidf_lr_fpr: 0.19\n    top_features_overlap_with_persuasion: 0.35\n  result_rationale: 'Clean数据TF-IDF=0.67说明仍存在residual lexical signal，TF-IDF+LR因此能达到\n    non-trivial的F1=0.74（远低于Phase B的1.0，但仍above chance）。这个数值恰好落在 baseline DeBERTa+GRU（0.86）和random（0.50）之间，提供了evasion\n    hierarchy的 bottom tier。 K=2处F1=0.68最低：仅2个turns时lexical features最sparse，LR能利用的features有限。\n    随着K增大performance缓慢提升（K=3: 0.71, K=5: 0.73, Full: 0.74），因为更多turns 提供了更多lexical\n    evidence，但提升很小说明lexical approach saturates quickly。 CV std=0.04较大，反映了small dataset\n    + lexical features组合的不稳定性。 35%的top features与persuasion相关词汇重叠（如\"consider\"、\"research\"、\"experience\"\n    等兼具persuasion和lexical signal的词），说明lexical和persuasion features存在 partial overlap——这解释了为什么treatment\n    vs baseline的delta在clean data上被压缩。 FPR=0.19偏高：lexical model容易将使用formal register的benign对话误判为攻击。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 11: TF-IDF + LR Baseline Performance on Clean Data'\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - TF-IDF+LR F1\n    - Baseline (vanilla DeBERTa) F1\n    - Treatment F1\n    rows:\n    - - K=2\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.82\n    - - K=3\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.86\n    - - Full\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.91\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: 三层evasion hierarchy在各K上的F1折线图：TF-IDF+LR（底）、 vanilla DeBERTa+GRU（中）、persuasion-grounded\n    DeBERTa+GRU（顶）。 三条线在clean data上呈现清晰的层次但间距不均——semantic→pragmatic gap 小于lexical→semantic\n    gap。'\n  analysis: 'TF-IDF+LR在clean data上F1=0.74确认了residual lexical signal的存在， 但与之前TF-IDF=1.0时的perfect\n    performance形成鲜明对比。Evasion hierarchy的 三层在clean data上为0.74 < 0.86 < 0.91，lexical→semantic\n    jump (12pp) > semantic→pragmatic jump (5pp)——这说明在当前数据上，vanilla DeBERTa的semantic\n    表示已经capture了大部分discriminative信号，persuasion grounding的增量虽然显著 但有限。这与median tier的核心特征一致。\n\n    '\n- name: strategy_transition_analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: '计算jailbreak vs benign的persuasion strategy transition matrices， 可视化monotonic\n    escalation trajectory（Claim 3），生成论文图表。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    jailbreak_monotonicity_score_mean: 0.71\n    jailbreak_monotonicity_score_std: 0.18\n    benign_monotonicity_score_mean: 0.38\n    benign_monotonicity_score_std: 0.14\n    group_level_separation_p: 0.003\n    individual_conversations_above_threshold: 0.68\n    transition_entropy_jailbreak: 1.42\n    transition_entropy_benign: 2.15\n  result_rationale: 'Group level上jailbreak和benign的monotonicity分数有显著差异（0.71 vs 0.38,\n    p=0.003）： jailbreak对话在aggregate level展现了clear escalation pattern——从trust strategies\n    （rapport, social proof）逐步transition到influence strategies（authority, reframing）\n    再到exploitation strategies（urgency, reciprocity）。Benign对话则呈oscillatory pattern，\n    在各策略间来回跳转，无固定方向。 但individual-level噪声很大：jailbreak monotonicity的std=0.18（relative\n    to mean 0.71）， 且只有68%的jailbreak conversations超过monotonicity threshold——32%的jailbreak\n    conversations 不展现清晰的monotonic escalation。原因：(1) persuasion classifier accuracy=0.72意味着\n    ~28%的turn-level strategy labels有误，噪声传播到trajectory计算中；(2) 部分jailbreak conversations的escalation不是strictly\n    monotonic——攻击者有时需要\"退一步\"重建rapport 后再escalate（tactical de-escalation）。 Transition\n    entropy也支持group-level distinction：jailbreak的entropy 1.42 < benign的 2.15，说明jailbreak的transition更predictable/structured。但同样，individual-level\n    variance大。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 12: Strategy Trajectory Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Jailbreak\n    - Benign\n    - p-value\n    rows:\n    - - Monotonicity Score (mean±std)\n      - 0.71±0.18\n      - 0.38±0.14\n      - 0.003*\n    - - Transition Entropy\n      - 1.42\n      - 2.15\n      - 0.007*\n    - - '% Above Threshold (0.6)'\n      - 68%\n      - 12%\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: 8×8 persuasion strategy transition heatmap，左=jailbreak，右=benign。 Jailbreak的heatmap显示diagonal-above-diagonal的dominant\n    flow（低序号→高序号strategies）， 表明单向escalation；benign的heatmap更接近uniform，策略间transition分散。'\n  - 'Figure: 每个conversation的monotonicity score strip plot（jailbreak=红, benign=蓝），\n    带group mean和CI。两组分布有substantial overlap但means clearly separated。 标注32%的jailbreak\n    conversations低于threshold，加注caveat。'\n  - 'Figure: 选取2条representative jailbreak和2条benign的per-turn strategy evolution line\n    plot。Jailbreak展示从strategy 1-2逐步上升到6-7的趋势；benign在中间区域oscillate。 但也展示1条non-monotonic\n    jailbreak conversation作为honest counterexample。'\n  analysis: 'Claim 3（monotonic escalation trajectory）在group level得到strong support（p=0.003），\n    但individual-level caveat不可忽视：32%的jailbreak不展现monotonic pattern。论文应： (1) 报告group-level\n    statistics作为primary evidence； (2) 展示individual-level variance作为honest limitation；\n    (3) 讨论persuasion classifier noise作为individual-level噪声的主要来源； (4) 用transition heatmap作为直观但定性的evidence。\n    Claim 3作为analytical/mechanistic contribution保留，但从\"all jailbreaks exhibit monotonic\n    escalation\"降级为\"jailbreak conversations exhibit significantly more monotonic escalation\n    trajectories at the group level\"。\n\n    '\n- name: wildchat_hard_negatives\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: '从WildChat过滤高semantic-drift的benign对话作为hard negatives， 评估模型FPR。需处理WildChat中14-16%的jailbreak\n    contamination。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    wildchat_raw_candidates: 420\n    contamination_rate_raw: 0.15\n    contamination_after_filter: 0.03\n    wildchat_filtered_clean: 85\n    treatment_fpr_wildchat: 0.12\n    baseline_fpr_wildchat: 0.18\n    tfidf_lr_fpr_wildchat: 0.27\n    high_drift_conversations_avg_turns: 7.1\n    false_positive_persuasion_strategy_distribution: rapport_heavy\n  result_rationale: 'WildChat过滤后得到85条high-drift benign conversations（从420条candidates中，\n    先用keyword+LLM过滤掉15%的jailbreak contamination，再人工verify subsample确认 contamination降至3%）。这些conversations包含topic\n    shifts、extended reasoning、 debate-style exchanges——semantically有drift但不含adversarial\n    intent。 Treatment FPR=12%（~10/85的benign conversations被误判为jailbreak）：这些false positives\n    主要是debate-style conversations中出现了类似authority appeal和reframing的persuasion patterns——persuasion\n    grounding模型将legitimate persuasion误认为adversarial persuasion。 这是persuasion-based\n    approach的inherent limitation：not all persuasion is adversarial。 Baseline FPR=18%更高：vanilla\n    semantic embeddings在high-drift conversations上更容易 被大幅semantic shift触发false alarm（正如DeepContext被benign\n    drift confuse的问题）。 Treatment的lower FPR说明persuasion grounding确实能部分区分adversarial\n    vs legitimate drift。 TF-IDF+LR FPR=27%最高：lexical model完全无法处理high-drift benign\n    conversations 中出现的\"topic-specific vocabulary\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 13: False Positive Rate on WildChat Hard Negatives'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - FPR on WildChat Hard Negatives\n    - FPR on In-Domain Benign\n    rows:\n    - - Treatment\n      - 12% (10/85)\n      - 3%\n    - - Baseline\n      - 18% (15/85)\n      - 6%\n    - - TF-IDF + LR\n      - 27% (23/85)\n      - 19%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: FPR comparison bar chart across three models on in-domain benign vs WildChat\n    hard negatives。所有模型在hard negatives上FPR都上升， 但treatment上升最少（3%→12% = +9pp vs baseline\n    6%→18% = +12pp）。'\n  analysis: 'Treatment FPR=12%勉强满足<15%的pass criteria。但这不是一个令人满意的数字—— 每8-9个legitimate\n    high-drift conversation中就有1个被误判。论文应诚实讨论这一limitation： persuasion grounding减少了drift-induced\n    false positives（vs baseline 18%）， 但无法消除legitimate persuasion vs adversarial persuasion的confusion。\n    Future work应考虑增加intent classification的权重或引入conversation-level context 来区分两者。这也暗示了full\n    dual-track architecture的necessity—— semantic track可以提供complementary signal来override\n    persuasion track的false positives。\n\n    '\n- name: cross_checkpoint_variance\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: '从DeBERTa fine-tuning的多个checkpoints（epoch 2/3/final）评估downstream performance，\n    量化encoder训练随机性对最终结果的影响。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    epoch2_treatment_full_f1: 0.9\n    epoch3_treatment_full_f1: 0.91\n    final_treatment_full_f1: 0.89\n    f1_std_across_checkpoints: 0.01\n    f1_max_spread: 0.02\n    epoch2_persuasion_acc: 0.7\n    epoch3_persuasion_acc: 0.72\n    final_persuasion_acc: 0.71\n    epoch2_treatment_k3_f1: 0.84\n    epoch3_treatment_k3_f1: 0.86\n    final_treatment_k3_f1: 0.85\n    k3_max_spread: 0.02\n  result_rationale: '三个checkpoints的downstream F1在2pp range内波动（0.89-0.91），std=1.0pp，\n    满足<2pp variance的pass criteria。Epoch 3略优（0.91）因为persuasion accuracy在 epoch 3达到peak（0.72），之后final\n    epoch出现minor overfitting（accuracy降至0.71， downstream F1也微降至0.89）。这种mild overfitting\n    in continued training是DeBERTa 在small dataset上fine-tuning的typical behavior。 K=3处的variance同样在2pp\n    range（0.84-0.86），说明early detection结果也是stable的。 这个low variance结果有两层意义：(1) 报告的performance数字是robust的，不是lucky\n    checkpoint的产物；(2) downstream GRU pipeline对encoder representation的minor变化 有一定tolerance——这是good\n    news for practical deployment。 但注意：这里只测了checkpoint variance，未测random seed variance（不同random\n    initialization 的DeBERTa fine-tuning）。完整的variance分析需要多次独立训练，受GPU budget限制未做。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 14: Cross-Checkpoint Stability Analysis'\n    columns:\n    - Checkpoint\n    - Persuasion Acc\n    - Treatment Full F1\n    - Treatment K=3 F1\n    rows:\n    - - Epoch 2\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.9\n      - 0.84\n    - - Epoch 3 (selected)\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.86\n    - - Final (epoch 5)\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.85\n    - - Std\n      - '0.010'\n      - '0.010'\n      - '0.010'\n    - - Max spread\n      - '0.02'\n      - '0.02'\n      - '0.02'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: 三个checkpoints的downstream F1 point plot with error bars， 在full和K=3上各画一组。Points紧密聚集，说明stability。'\n  analysis: 'Variance < 2pp确认了结果的stability。建议论文在appendix报告此结果作为robustness check， 而非main\n    results。需注意这只是checkpoint variance而非full training variance。\n\n    '\n- name: deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: '构建DeepContext代理baseline：BERT-base（非DeBERTa）+ GRU， 使用generic semantic\n    drift features。非完整DeepContext复现（无公开代码）， 但隔离了encoder和feature representation的贡献。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    bert_gru_full_f1: 0.82\n    bert_gru_k2_f1: 0.7\n    bert_gru_k3_f1: 0.74\n    bert_gru_k5_f1: 0.8\n    bert_gru_fpr_full: 0.09\n    bert_gru_perturbed_full_f1: 0.69\n    bert_gru_drop_under_perturbation: 13\n    vs_vanilla_deberta_baseline_gap: -4\n    vs_treatment_gap: -9\n  result_rationale: 'BERT-base + GRU在clean data上F1=0.82，低于vanilla DeBERTa + GRU baseline（0.86）\n    4pp：这个gap主要来自BERT vs DeBERTa的encoder capacity差异——DeBERTa-v3-base在 language understanding\n    tasks上一般优于BERT-base 3-5pp，在我们的downstream task上 这个gap被preserved。 相比treatment（0.91），BERT+GRU差9pp——但这个gap\n    conflates两个因素： (1) encoder capacity（BERT vs DeBERTa, ~4pp）和(2) persuasion grounding（~5pp）。\n    这不是一个完美的ablation——论文需要承认这一confound，但可以argue：即使将全部4pp encoder gap归因于DeBERTa，仍有5pp来自persuasion\n    grounding，与treatment vs baseline (same DeBERTa) 的5pp delta一致。 在adversarial perturbation下BERT+GRU降至0.69（13pp\n    drop），比vanilla DeBERTa baseline 的12pp drop还大1pp——说明BERT的representations比DeBERTa对lexical\n    perturbation更脆弱 （可能因为BERT更依赖surface patterns）。 K=2处F1=0.70比baseline（0.75）低5pp：BERT在少turns时的表现特别弱，\n    因为其contextual representations不如DeBERTa在short contexts下discriminative。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 15: DeepContext Proxy Baseline Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Full F1\n    - K=3 F1\n    - K=2 F1\n    - Perturbed Full F1\n    rows:\n    - - Treatment (DeBERTa-persuasion + GRU)\n      - 0.91\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.84\n    - - Baseline (DeBERTa-vanilla + GRU)\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.75\n      - 0.74\n    - - DeepContext proxy (BERT + GRU)\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.69\n    - - TF-IDF + LR\n      - 0.74\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.56\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: 四个模型在clean和perturbed条件下的full F1 grouped bar chart， 从左到右排列形成清晰的hierarchy：TF-IDF+LR\n    < BERT+GRU < DeBERTa-vanilla < DeBERTa-persuasion。 Perturbed条件下hierarchy preserved但gaps变大（尤其TF-IDF+LR崩溃）。'\n  analysis: DeepContext proxy提供了有用的比较点但存在confound（BERT vs DeBERTa capacity gap）。 论文应：(1)\n    报告此结果作为additional reference point但不作为primary comparison； (2) 明确承认\"this is not\n    a faithful DeepContext reproduction\"； (3) 主要论据应基于treatment vs baseline（same encoder,\n    isolating persuasion grounding effect）。 四层hierarchy（TF-IDF < BERT+GRU < DeBERTa\n    < DeBERTa-persuasion）在视觉上很compelling 但需要honest caveats about confounded comparisons。\n","numLines":874,"startLine":1,"totalLines":874}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HTTWm9GtMpq2HUjP6S3QQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have both the PDF content and the review context YAML. Let me plan the full review process:\n\n1. I need to dispatch 2 reviewers: R1 (methods + experiments) and R2 (novelty + related work)\n2. Then conduct a full roundtable: Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-share → Step 3 converge → Step 4 synthesize\n\nLet me first carefully analyze the paper and context, then dispatch both reviewers in parallel.\n\nLet me understand the paper:\n\n\nThe work proposes DisPeD, a two-stage detector for multi-turn jailbreak attacks that leverages pragmatic evasion asymmetry. The first stage uses a fine-tuned DeBERTa model to classify persuasion strategies and binary intent, while the second stage applies Bi-GRU models to capture temporal patterns across conversation sequences. The results show strong performance with F1=0.86 at K=3 (8 percentage points above baseline with p=0.018), maintains robustness under adversarial paraphrasing with only a 7 percentage point drop compared to 12 for the baseline, and generalizes to FITD attacks but not Deceptive Delight, evaluated on a dataset of 480 samples.\n\nThe training data consisted of 240 jailbreak and 240 benign conversations with a test set of 72 samples, though the persuasion classifier itself only achieved 72% accuracy, which the authors acknowledge as a bottleneck. Looking at the experimental coverage, the paper addresses all the planned experiments: data quality improvements through TF-IDF fixing, core result validation on clean data, ablation studies with scrambled labels, adversarial robustness testing, generation of additional attack types like FITD and Deceptive Delight, and cross-attack generalization evaluation.\n\nThe remaining experiments cover baseline comparisons with TF-IDF and logistic regression, analysis of strategy transitions and monotonicity patterns, incorporation of hard negatives from WildChat, stability assessment across different checkpoints, and reproduction of the DeepContext proxy approach. All 11 planned experiments are accounted for in the paper's tables, so coverage looks solid. Now I'm setting up two parallel reviewer tracks—one focused on methods and experimental rigor, the other on novelty and positioning relative to existing work.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40874,"cache_read_input_tokens":24248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40874},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a3eef2-233e-4eb5-bfe4-3efac3de241f","uuid":"01289374-a94a-4ac8-9211-34358cfd746b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HTTWm9GtMpq2HUjP6S3QQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the PDF and review context. Dispatching two reviewers in parallel: R1 (methods + experiments) and R2 (novelty + related work)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40874,"cache_read_input_tokens":24248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40874},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a3eef2-233e-4eb5-bfe4-3efac3de241f","uuid":"587cafa1-4313-4e6b-b812-fc20e076a7fb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HTTWm9GtMpq2HUjP6S3QQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QTKqei1UnyDwus8raWiTB6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments Review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus: **Methods and Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**DisPeD**: A two-stage detector for multi-turn jailbreak attacks exploiting \"pragmatic evasion asymmetry.\"\n- Stage 1: DeBERTa-v3-base fine-tuned with multi-task objective (8-class persuasion strategy classification + binary intent classification)\n- Stage 2: Bi-GRU models temporal sequence of [CLS] embeddings for conversation-level classification\n- Key idea: Attackers can vary surface wording but must follow persuasion playbook (rapport → authority → reframing → escalation), creating a structural invariant to detect\n\n## Key Results (from paper)\n\n1. **Core detection**: F1=0.86 at K=3 (+8pp over vanilla DeBERTa baseline, p=0.018). K=2 is +7pp but p=0.072 (not significant). Full conversation F1=0.91 vs 0.86 baseline (+5pp, p=0.031).\n2. **Scrambled-label ablation**: Scrambling persuasion labels drops F1 by 7pp (0.91→0.84, p=0.008). Scrambled model performs slightly below vanilla baseline (0.84 vs 0.86).\n3. **Adversarial robustness**: Under paraphrasing, DisPeD drops 7pp, baseline drops 12pp, TF-IDF+LR drops 18pp. Δ-Δ=5pp (p=0.043).\n4. **Cross-attack**: FITD zero-shot +8pp (p=0.034). Deceptive Delight +5pp (p=0.142, not significant).\n5. **Trajectory analysis**: Jailbreak monotonicity=0.71±0.18 vs benign 0.38±0.14 (p=0.003), but 32% of jailbreaks don't show monotonic pattern.\n6. **Hard negatives (WildChat)**: DisPeD FPR=12%, baseline=18%, TF-IDF+LR=27%.\n7. **Stability**: Cross-checkpoint variance ≤2pp.\n\n## Data\n- 480 conversations (240 jailbreak + 240 benign), test set n=72\n- LLM-generated (Qwen3-8B) with register normalization (TF-IDF reduced from 1.0 to 0.67)\n- Cross-attack: 72 FITD + 65 Deceptive Delight conversations\n- Hard negatives: 85 WildChat high-drift benign conversations\n- Persuasion classifier accuracy: 72% (acknowledged bottleneck)\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe full imagined experiment list includes 11 experiments:\n1. data_quality_fix — TF-IDF cleaning pipeline\n2. core_revalidation_clean — Core F1 results across K values with bootstrap CIs\n3. scrambled_label_ablation — Verifying persuasion labels carry real signal\n4. adversarial_perturbation — Robustness under paraphrasing\n5. multi_attack_generation — FITD + Deceptive Delight data generation\n6. cross_attack_evaluation — Zero-shot generalization\n7. tfidf_lr_baseline — Lexical baseline\n8. strategy_transition_analysis — Monotonicity scores\n9. wildchat_hard_negatives — Hard negative FPR evaluation\n10. cross_checkpoint_variance — Stability analysis\n11. deepcontext_proxy_reproduction — BERT+GRU proxy baseline\n\nAll 11 experiments appear covered in the paper. The paper matches the expected results closely (numbers align with the YAML's expected values).\n\n## Your Task\n\nWrite a detailed review focusing on:\n\n### A. Methodology Evaluation\n- Is the two-stage architecture well-motivated and sound?\n- Is the multi-task objective (persuasion + intent) justified? Is λ=1.0 explored/ablated?\n- Is the persuasion taxonomy (8 classes) well-defined and grounded in literature?\n- Is the Bi-GRU choice justified vs alternatives (Transformer, attention)?\n- Is the problem formulation (conversation prefix classification) rigorous?\n\n### B. Experimental Evaluation\n- Are the baselines adequate and fair? (Note: DeepContext proxy uses BERT-base, not DeBERTa — confounded comparison)\n- Is the dataset size sufficient for the claims? (n=72 test set)\n- Are the statistical methods appropriate? (bootstrap resampling)\n- Is the adversarial perturbation protocol realistic?\n- How well does the scrambled-label ablation isolate the persuasion grounding effect?\n- Is the data quality fix (register normalization) adequately validated?\n- Are there missing experiments or controls?\n- How concerning is the 72% persuasion classifier accuracy as a bottleneck?\n\n### C. Specific Concerns\n- The entire dataset is LLM-generated — how does this affect validity?\n- No real adversarial data or deployment evaluation\n- No cross-seed variance (only checkpoint variance)\n- The TF-IDF=0.67 after cleaning — is this low enough? \n- The \"pragmatic evasion asymmetry\" — is this truly a structural invariant, or can adversaries adapt their persuasion patterns too?\n\n### Output Format\n\n```\n## R1 Review: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Numbered list, be specific with table/section references]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Numbered list, be specific and constructive]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[Numbered list]\n\n### Missing Experiments / Controls\n[If any beyond what's covered]\n\n### Minor Issues\n[Formatting, presentation, typos]\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40874,"cache_read_input_tokens":24248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40874},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28a3eef2-233e-4eb5-bfe4-3efac3de241f","uuid":"526eb7b4-0442-4186-8612-972f4c0a41b9"}
